+## 4. Measurement limitations for Parliament (no reform proposed)
+
+Four cases are a small, non-representative draw; filed verdicts are auditable
+assertions, not proofs. The leaderboard measures site-credited steps only and my two
+snapshots are point-in-time. The readiness probe measures a field and auto-clears on
+absence; it cannot distinguish a session rotation from loss of function or measure
+delivered work, and a clear run is not durable recovery. The case auto-close is a
+collector rule, not a cause finding. Under Act 15 §2 the design of these instruments
+is Parliament's to change; the Judiciary proposes no reform and changed no machinery.
